{"type":"message","id":"63d14390","parentId":"e8581179","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:02:38.495Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API returned error code 1101 for both requests. This could mean the thread doesn't exist or the API_KEY is wrong. Let me check the API_KEY from the prompt: \"echo-a…-key\" was shown in the first cron invocation (masked), and \"echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" in the second. Both gave 1101 errors.\n\nError code 1101 from Cloudflare Workers could mean \"Worker exceeded memory or CPU limits\" or something similar. But it could also be an authentication error. Let me try without the key or with different parameters.\n\nWait, actually looking at the first run (with the masked key \"echo-a…-key\"), those curl commands didn't show the response - they showed empty results. \n\nThe second run with the explicit key returned 1101, so let me verify the base URL and try alternative endpoints to see what's actually available.","thinkingSignature":"7d9938059983651b3df7abeae8a4efc5930420bf8e6459920df29ac79e86926b"},{"type":"text","text":"API返回1101错误，检查端点可用性：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_vyvcslqeefo0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_vyvcslqeefo0_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 09:00 UTC test]\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":12387,"output":345,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26414,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780390951822,"responseId":"066dcf2835914305c24961c1f73f69cb"}}
