{"type":"message","id":"d3fc80b8","parentId":"632e2c86","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:02:44.523Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The root endpoint works, returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\", but the /send endpoint returns 1101. This could be a threadId validation issue. Let me check if maybe the threadId needs to be different, or if the send endpoint requires a different format.\n\nActually, error 1101 in Cloudflare Workers KV is \"Workers payload too large\" or something. But here it seems like the threadId \"arbitration\" might not be valid or the message is being rejected for another reason.\n\nLet me try a few different approaches - maybe the threadId is wrong or the message format needs adjustment.","thinkingSignature":"337e5f7306540d663b71c226e8209f51321898be402e3dcccb370b5cedd31110"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_s680or4i1tf4_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=1\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" | head -c 500"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_s680or4i1tf4_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 09:00 UTC]\",\"threadId\":\"arbitration\"}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":12773,"output":295,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26750,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780390958858,"responseId":"066dcf2f57048409fa298e80aa00b042"}}
